{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310853,"nonce":"88Vq4FggQacpZSKy67hl6ueXNGw=","title":"Synthetic 2-layer/16-hidden Llama-style smoke test at nue/examples/tiny-transformer. Three of four blocker bugs fixed (c1e2537 + ed80d75 + ...","message":"Run from a clean cache:\n\n```bash\ncd nue/examples/tiny-transformer \u0026\u0026 rm -rf .rayzor\nrayzor run Main.hx\n```\n\nReaches:\n```\n[build] LlamaModel hidden=16 layers=2 heads=2/1 ffn=32\n[forward] ids=[1, 2, 3] -\u003e logits=[3,8]           # ← 2-block forward OK\n```\n\n…and then SIGBUSes inside `GenerationLoop.generate` → `tokenizer.encode(prompt)`.\nProbing narrower: even a DIRECT (concrete) `tok.encode(\"t1\")` call right after\nconstructing the BPETokenizer crashes the same way:\n\n```haxe\nvar tok = new BPETokenizer(vocab, [], false);\ntrace(\"[main] BPETokenizer built\");          // prints\nvar direct = tok.encode(\"t1\");                // SIGBUS\n```\n\nSo the remaining bug is *not* interface dispatch — `tok` is concretely\ntyped `BPETokenizer`. It's BPETokenizer.encode itself, on a trivially-\nconstructed instance with empty `merges` and a tiny `Vocab`. Could be\nthe byte-level branch reading garbage at field 5, the rankIndex empty-\nStringMap iteration, or something else in the encode body.\n\n\n- **c1e2537** — Same-context constructor args route through\n  `maybe_materialize_for_call`; HIR ctor params don't include `this`,\n  so user `args[i]` lines up with HIR param index `i` (not `i + 1`).\n  Tensor row-broadcast in `tensor_mul`/`add`/`sub` for RMSNorm gain.\n- **ed80d75** — `BladeFuncEntry.param_type_names: Vec\u003cOption\u003cString\u003e\u003e`\n  persists per-param Class/Interface qualified names in the BLADE\n  cache. Restored + renumbered into\n  `import_function_param_iface_names`, threaded through to\n  `HirToMirContext::external_function_param_iface_names`. A Path 3\n  fallback resolves names to current-context SymbolIds and runs the\n  fat-pointer wrap.\n- **3aebe8f** — The Path 3 fallback also drops any pre-cached\n  `interface_vtables[(class, iface)]` before wrapping. Cached entries\n  from sibling files contain method SymbolIds that aren't stable\n  across compilation contexts.\n- **a1fc8bd** — `LlamaModel.resetCache` uses concrete `cast(block,\n  TransformerBlock)` + `cast(tb.attn, GQAttention)` instead of\n  `var tb:Dynamic = block; tb.attn.cache.reset()`. Dynamic field\n  access on an interface fat pointer reads the obj_ptr at offset 0 as\n  a class type-id and dispatches into garbage.\n- **8b4f3c9** — `maybe_unbox_value` skips `haxe_unbox_reference_ptr`\n  when the value's MIR type is already `Ptr(_)` and the target is\n  `Array`/`Interface`/`Anonymous`. Cross-file interface dispatch\n  marks the call_indirect result HIR type as `Dynamic` (the actual\n  return type doesn't propagate cleanly across contexts), and the\n  unbox path treated the raw `HaxeArray *` as a `DynamicValue`\n  pointer — reading `value_ptr` returned garbage and SIGBUSed on the\n  next field access.\n\n\n1. **Debug BPETokenizer.encode on a trivial instance.** Direct call,\n   not interface dispatch — concrete `BPETokenizer`. Likely candidates:\n   - The byte-level branch read at field 5 (Bool) — `gep bool` actually\n     strides by 8 in the cranelift backend (per\n     [cranelift_backend.rs:3213-3218](compiler/src/codegen/cranelift_backend.rs#L3213-L3218)),\n     so the read is correct, but the value at field 5 may be garbage if\n     the constructor's storage didn't normalize the byte.\n   - StringMap iteration on an empty rankIndex.\n   - Vocab encoding logic with a non-byte-level path that's never\n     exercised in the GGUF e2e (which uses byte_level=true).\n2. Once encode runs, expect a similar interface-method-return-type\n   propagation issue for `model.forwardIds(ids)` → `Tensor`. The\n   8b4f3c9 fix should cover that too, but verify.\n3. After tokenizer + forwardIds work, `sampler.sample(lastRow(logits))`\n   is the next dispatch — same pattern, should be covered.\n\n\nThe pattern these fixes unlock: cross-file `Array\u003cModule\u003e`, interface-\ntyped class fields, interface methods returning `Array\u003cT\u003e` — all work.\nWhat still doesn't work: Dynamic field access on interface fat pointers\n(use concrete downcasts instead — see commit a1fc8bd), and any pre-\nexisting stdlib bug exercised only by the smoke test (e.g. the encode\ncrash above).\n\nWhen adding ML-layer features in nue, **don't use `Dynamic` to reach\ninto interface-typed fields**. Either downcast concretely or add a\nmethod to the interface. The compiler will not unwrap the fat pointer\nthrough Dynamic — that path was discussed and rejected in the smoke-\ntest thread because it'd leak interface ABI into Dynamic semantics.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_nue_tiny_transformer_smoke` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}